{"The awaited dynamic import should be wrapped in a try/catch so that a failed module load produces a meaningful error message (e.g., which `dirName` failed) instead of an opaque rejection propagating to the caller (handlePayment.ts).": 0.17397156357765198, "`async` callbacks inside `forEach` are fire-and-forget \u2014 the returned promises are never awaited, so the `try/catch` block cannot catch rejections and the deletions race with the subsequent email send. Use `Promise.all` with `.map` (or a `for...of` loop) to properly await each operation.": 0.9531975984573364, "Changing `getCalendar` to `async` breaks the synchronous caller `getCalendarCredentials` in `CalendarManager.ts`. It calls `getCalendar(credential)` inside a `.flatMap()` callback without awaiting, so the `calendar` field will be an unresolved `Promise` instead of the actual `Calendar` instance. This will silently break calendar operations at runtime. The caller needs to be converted to use `Promise.all` or an equivalent async pattern.": 0.7515600323677063, "All `import()` calls execute eagerly at module load time since they're direct expressions in the object literal\u2014this doesn't achieve lazy loading. Every property is now a `Promise<module>` that fires immediately, loading all 28 modules in parallel as soon as this file is imported. Wrap them in thunks to defer loading until actually needed.": 0.9108632802963257}